## What Problem This Solves

After a macOS reboot, a stale Codex app-server registration can point at a reused parent PID that this process cannot inspect. That permission error blocks new Codex app-server starts even when the registered child is already gone.

Fixes #203395

## Why This Change Was Made

On Darwin, when inspecting the recorded parent and child fails with a permission error, the sweep checks the child alone. It removes the registration only when the child is absent from that snapshot and `kill(pid, 0)` returns `ESRCH`.

This preserves the existing `readDarwinProcessSnapshot()` contract: missing PIDs are omitted, while inspection errors still fail closed.

## User Impact

Codex app-server turns can start again after reboot when the registered child is confirmed absent; an existing or unreadable child remains fail-closed.

## Evidence

- Production module boundary: the real `prepareCodexAppServerProcessRegistration()` entrypoint used its SQLite state store and native macOS process inspection with the same command and input on base and head.
- Base `ae8155cf5f5434132b578504716a60c62c3de4e6`: absent child and live-child control both failed with `permission`; both registrations remained.
- Head `27d1e6a493fde934785da1bb347fceaede8a735f`: the absent child registration was cleared; the live-child control remained rejected with `permission` and preserved its registration.
- Exact tested head SHA: `27d1e6a493fde934785da1bb347fceaede8a735f`.
- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-database-workers.config.ts codex/src/app-server/transport-process-registration.test.ts` — 11 tests passed.

```text
$ node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs .artifacts/proof-live-203395.mts
before: base ae8155cf5f5434132b578504716a60c62c3de4e6 — {"parentPid":1,"absent":{"label":"stale-registration-with-absent-child","status":"rejected","reason":"permission","preserved":true},"control":{"label":"stale-registration-with-live-child-control","status":"rejected","reason":"permission","preserved":true}}
after: head 27d1e6a493fde934785da1bb347fceaede8a735f — {"parentPid":1,"absent":{"label":"stale-registration-with-absent-child","status":"fulfilled","preserved":false},"control":{"label":"stale-registration-with-live-child-control","status":"rejected","reason":"permission","preserved":true}}
negative-control: live child remained rejected with permission and its registration was preserved.
```

<details>
<summary>Reproduce the macOS process-boundary proof</summary>

Save this as `.artifacts/proof-live-203395.mts` and run the command above from the repository root.

```ts
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { mkdtemp, rm } from "node:fs/promises";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { spawn } from "node:child_process";
import { createPluginStateSyncKeyedStore } from "openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-state-store-runtime";
import { prepareCodexAppServerProcessRegistration } from "../extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-process-registration.js";

const options = {
  namespace: "app-server-processes",
  maxEntries: 512,
  overflowPolicy: "reject-new",
} as const;

async function runCase(childPid: number, label: string) {
  const root = await mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "codex-203395-proof-"));
  const previous = process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR;
  process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR = root;
  const store = createPluginStateSyncKeyedStore<{
    parent: { pid: number; pgid: number; startedAt: string };
    child: {
      pid: number;
      pgid: number;
      startedAt: string;
      commandFingerprint: string;
    };
  }>("codex", options);
  const command = "/opt/codex app-server --listen stdio://";
  const startedAt = "Thu Jan 1 00:00:00 1970";
  store.register("stale-parent", {
    parent: { pid: 1, pgid: 1, startedAt },
    child: {
      pid: childPid,
      pgid: childPid,
      startedAt,
      commandFingerprint: createHash("sha256").update(command).digest("hex"),
    },
  });

  let status = "fulfilled";
  let reason: string | undefined;
  try {
    await prepareCodexAppServerProcessRegistration();
  } catch (error) {
    status = "rejected";
    reason = error && typeof error === "object" && "reason" in error
      ? String(error.reason)
      : error instanceof Error
        ? error.name
        : "unknown";
  }
  const preserved = store.lookup("stale-parent") !== undefined;
  store.clear();
  await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });
  if (previous === undefined) {
    delete process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR;
  } else {
    process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR = previous;
  }
  return { label, status, reason, preserved };
}

async function createExitedPid(): Promise<number> {
  const child = spawn("/bin/sleep", ["60"], { stdio: "ignore" });
  await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
    child.once("spawn", resolve);
    child.once("error", reject);
  });
  const pid = child.pid;
  if (!pid) throw new Error("sleep child did not receive a PID");
  child.kill("SIGTERM");
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => child.once("exit", () => resolve()));
  try {
    process.kill(pid, 0);
    throw new Error("exited child PID unexpectedly remains live");
  } catch (error) {
    if ((error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== "ESRCH") throw error;
  }
  return pid;
}

async function createLivePid() {
  const child = spawn("/bin/sleep", ["60"], { stdio: "ignore" });
  await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
    child.once("spawn", resolve);
    child.once("error", reject);
  });
  if (!child.pid) throw new Error("sleep child did not receive a PID");
  return child;
}

const absentPid = await createExitedPid();
const absent = await runCase(absentPid, "stale-registration-with-absent-child");
const live = await createLivePid();
let control;
try {
  control = await runCase(live.pid!, "stale-registration-with-live-child-control");
} finally {
  live.kill("SIGTERM");
}
console.log(JSON.stringify({ parentPid: 1, absent, control }));
```

</details>

