## What Problem This Solves

Large configured fleets can make Gateway model-catalog reads repeatedly hash the same runtime config while resolving prepared owners.

Fixes #195819

## Why This Change Was Made

Reuse config fingerprints only inside one synchronous Gateway catalog batch. Each later batch gets a fresh cache, so config changes cannot reuse stale comparisons.

## User Impact

Fleet catalog reads avoid redundant config serialization while preserving the prepared owner and model selection after reloads.

## Evidence

- Pinned rebase base: `b7bf937423f65c313c8fe98b81b112537286ecaf`. Main had removed the old 758-line owner-selection suite; that deletion stays intact. The PR's new 128-agent Gateway regression now lives in the existing `prepared-model-runtime.catalog-owner.test.ts` suite (32/32 tests pass), with exactly 2 config hashes per batch and 2 fresh hashes after config mutation.
- To satisfy the owner module's 700-line cap, batch-scoped cache logic lives in `src/agents/prepared-model-runtime.read-batch.ts`; the original `withPreparedModelRuntimeReadBatch` export remains available through the owner module.
- Historical base control on `cdfda39e4aa4461ecda7d6b2c63cb7a39d975d3e`: the same regression used 256 hashes instead of 2.
- Exact-head Gateway RPC proof on `2e42db17d5dda03fc0bb0c26515990c675224de5`: health reached `coreReady=true`; two metadata-only file reloads were accepted; `agents.list` returned 16 unique IDs/workspaces and identical model selections across both revisions.
- `pnpm check:test-lines-ratchet --base b7bf937423f65c313c8fe98b81b112537286ecaf --no-merge-base`: passed with +49 net test lines and 50 lines of issue allocation; the shared baseline is unchanged.
- Exact-head line-cap ratchet and formatting checks passed for the owner module, extracted batch module, and catalog-owner test.

