## What Problem This Solves

Retrying an npm update from 2026.9.37 after a rollback can fail when live Doctor cannot acquire the agent database maintenance lease.

## User Impact

The retry can migrate the restored profile and start the updated Gateway.

## Why This Change Was Made

Doctor configures shared SQLite journaling after verifying the captured database and before taking exclusive access. After the migration releases that lock, the agent maintenance worker can write to the shared database.

## Evidence

- With rollback-journal SQLite headers, the published 2026.9.37 updater hit the lease error in live Doctor on main (`3435fb5`). The database and package rollback returned schemas 19/24 and the original build. The PR head (`288c4f0`) retried the same profile after that rollback, with no other test updates running, and migrated the shared and agent schemas to 41/43.
- On the PR head, fresh updates from 2026.9.37, 2026.10.10, and 2026.11.6 also reached schemas 41/43. The loopback Gateway became ready and the Workboard card and workspace file survived all four successful updates.
- The 2026.9.37 regression failed on main with SQLite error 5 and passed on the PR head. It adds 12 test lines to exercise a second writer while Doctor retains the migrated connection.
- Six focused test files ran on macOS in 6m 53s, with 155 passes and five Linux-only skips. Targeted lint, format, core typecheck, and the test-line budget passed. Independent Codex source review found no P0–P2 issue in the migration and locking paths.

